    {
      "name": "Observe Weakness",
      "category": "action",
      "placement": "bot",
      "activity": {
        "unit": "action",
        "number": 1,
        "symbol": "◆"
      },
      "traits": [
        "concentrate",
        "divination",
        "fortune",
        "occult"
      ],
      "entries": [
        "Okoro studies a creature within 30 feet to find an opening to attack. On his next attack roll against the creature this turn, he rolls twice and uses the higher result, and his attack gains the fortune trait. The target becomes temporarily immune for 1d4 rounds."
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Push My Luck",
      "category": "reaction",
      "placement": "bot",
      "activity": {
        "unit": "reaction",
        "number": 1,
        "symbol": "◈"
      },
      "traits": [],
      "entries": [
        "Okoro draws upon his future luck to guarantee his attack. When he makes his attack roll, if he rolls lower than 10 on the die, he treats that attack roll as a 10 instead. This is in addition to rolling twice and taking the higher result from Observe Weakness. Afterward, Okoro's luck is temporarily spent, and he must roll twice and use the lower result of his next 3 checks; this is a misfortune effect. He can't use Push My Luck again until he's completed these 3 checks."
      ],
      "trigger": "Okoro targets a creature with an attack",
      "requirements": "The triggering creature was the target of Observe Weakness this turn"
    },
    {
      "name": "Rupture Shadow",
      "category": "action",
      "placement": "bot",
      "activity": {
        "unit": "action",
        "number": 2,
        "symbol": "◆◆"
      },
      "traits": [
        "acid",
        "conjuration",
        "occult",
        "shadow"
      ],
      "entries": [
        "Okoro can create immense blisters on a creature's shadow, which immediately burst, dealing 20d6 acid damage. He targets a creature within 60 feet that is casting a shadow, which must attempt a DC 37 Will save. Okoro can't use Rupture Shadow again for 1d4 rounds."
      ],
